ACC-018 — Engineering Explainability

Document ID: ACC-018
Title: Engineering Explainability
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification defines Engineering Explainability, the capability of the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF) to communicate the rationale underlying engineering cognition, conclusions, recommendations, and decision support.

Engineering Explainability enables engineers, stakeholders, regulators, and external systems to understand why engineering conclusions were reached and how supporting evidence, understanding, reasoning, and constraints contributed to those conclusions.

2. Scope

This specification applies to all engineering cognition and outputs generated within Atlas.

Engineering Explainability applies to:

Engineering Evidence
Engineering Understanding
Engineering Memory
Engineering Knowledge
Engineering Reasoning
Engineering Capability outputs
Engineering recommendations
Decision Support
Engineering conclusions

Explainability applies throughout the engineering cognition lifecycle.

3. Canonical Definition

Engineering Explainability is the capability to communicate the reasoning, evidence, assumptions, constraints, context, and knowledge that justify engineering conclusions and recommendations.

Explainability answers why an engineering conclusion is justified.

It complements Engineering Traceability, which answers where the supporting information originated.

4. Characteristics

Engineering Explainability SHALL possess the following characteristics.

4.1 Understandable

Engineering explanations SHALL be understandable by their intended audience while preserving technical accuracy.

4.2 Evidence-Based

Engineering explanations SHALL reference supporting Engineering Evidence.

4.3 Context-Aware

Engineering explanations SHALL include relevant Engineering Context and Engineering Intent.

4.4 Reasoning-Oriented

Engineering explanations SHALL describe the engineering reasoning that produced the conclusion.

4.5 Constraint-Aware

Engineering explanations SHALL identify Engineering Constraints that materially influenced the conclusion.

4.6 Confidence-Aware

Engineering explanations SHALL communicate Engineering Confidence where applicable.

4.7 Traceable

Engineering explanations SHALL maintain traceability to the engineering artifacts upon which they are based.

